  "narrative": "The independent validation for H5 is strong and supports the accepted SMARCA4-loss association. R26 gives a signed estimate of 0.852 with an independently adjusted interval from 0.765 to 0.939. Because H5 is registered in the negative direction, this signed positive result means the raw SMARCA4-loss minus SMARCA4-wild-type contrast is approximately -0.852: SMARCA4-loss samples have a substantially lower, more negative dependency_composite score, corresponding to stronger dependency. The entire validation interval exceeds the 0.15-unit meaningful-effect threshold, is consistent with discovery R5 (signed 0.804; CI 0.742 to 0.866), and is reinforced by the conditional estimates within TP53 wild-type, KEAP1 wild-type, adenocarcinoma, TP53-loss, and KEAP1-loss contexts. Therefore H5 remains accepted and now has both discovery and independent validation evidence in the supplied dataset. The current dataset-supported main-effect picture is: TP53 loss is associated with a higher, less negative composite score/weaker dependency (H13, discovery only so far); KEAP1 loss is associated with a higher composite score/weaker dependency (H4, validated); and SMARCA4 loss is associated with a lower composite score/stronger dependency (H5, now validated). Negative or unsupported registered findings include the original negative TP53 direction (H1), the KRAS and STK11 negative main-effect claims (H2 and H3), ARID1A (H6), arbitrary research markers D/E/F (H7-H9), media serum level (H10), matched RNA/DNA availability (H11), and the positive KEAP1-by-hypoxia interaction (H47). These are not proof of no association in any direction or subgroup, only that the specified meaningful effects are not supported. The most important unresolved questions remain whether the three robust associations interact additively or context-dependently. The most informative next analyses are formal interactions among core predictors, especially KEAP1-by-SMARCA4, together with the already registered TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 and STK11 interaction tests, and the triple-wild-type estimates H55-H57. If those interactions are near zero while triple-wild-type estimates remain large, the evidence will support relatively broad additive associations within this dataset; if a meaningful interaction appears, it will motivate subgroup-specific interpretation. All conclusions remain observational associations in the supplied dataset, not causal claims or demonstrated generalizable biological mechanisms.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence summary. Accepted validated associations: H4 KEAP1 loss higher dependency_composite (weaker dependency): discovery R4 0.810 [0.745,0.875], validation R13 0.784 [0.697,0.871]; H5 SMARCA4 loss lower dependency_composite (stronger dependency): discovery R5 signed 0.804 [0.742,0.866], validation R26 signed 0.852 [0.765,0.939]. Accepted unvalidated strong association: H13 TP53 loss higher dependency_composite (weaker dependency): discovery R1 signed 0.829 [0.767,0.891], with robust conditional means in KEAP1 WT (R15), adenocarcinoma (R19), KEAP1-loss background (R21). Robust conditional claims accepted active: H31, H34, H36, H37, H39, H40, H41, H43, H44, H45, H46. Rejected/closed: H1 (TP53 original negative direction opposite evidence), H2-H11 registered main effects not supported, H47 KEAP1 positive hypoxia interaction rejected because signed estimate -0.007 [ -0.137,0.124]. Deferred unresolved: H12 KRAS-STK11 interaction underpowered/wide. Registered but untested priorities: formal interactions H14,H15,H18,H19,H21,H22,H23,H16,H17,H20,H48,H49,H50; triple WT main estimates H55,H56,H57; technical predictors H29,H30,H52; other lesions H51,H53,H54; newly proposed KEAP1-by-SMARCA4 interaction. Next analysis should focus on additive versus context-specific behavior of the three accepted predictors, especially pairwise interactions among TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/STK11 and triple-wild-type estimates. Consider validating H13 if interactions remain consistent and no conflicting conditional evidence appears. Avoid causal or generalizable language; retain arbitrary markers/signatures and technical predictors as confounding/context only unless strong robust evidence emerges."
